RupeeRise – Corrected Investor Brief

Company: RupeeRise (Fictional Digital Lending App)
Location: Bengaluru, India

India’s Digital Payments Opportunity

India’s digital payments ecosystem provides an important foundation for technology-enabled financial services. According to NPCI, UPI processed 25.47 billion transactions worth approximately ₹31.53 lakh crore in October 2026, with 758 banks live on the platform. These figures demonstrate the scale of India’s digital payment infrastructure. NPCI – UPI Statistics

The adoption base is also expanding. The Ministry of Finance reported 55.49 crore users onboarded on UPI by June 2026. During FY2025–26, UPI recorded 24,161.69 crore transactions, worth ₹314.23 lakh crore. Transaction volume increased by approximately 30% compared with FY2024–25. PIB – UPI Statistics

For RupeeRise, this digital infrastructure represents an opportunity to explore convenient, transparent and responsible digital credit services. However, UPI adoption figures should not be treated as digital-lending market size or as the number of potential borrowers.

Regulatory Framework

RupeeRise must work within the applicable RBI regulatory framework. The RBI (Digital Lending) Directions, 2025 (RBI/2025-26/36) require regulated entities to provide a Key Fact Statement (KFS) under the applicable RBI KFS instructions, including relevant APR disclosures. They also require loan disbursal and repayment to follow prescribed bank-account flows, restricting third-party pass-through accounts, subject to specified exceptions.

The regulated lender remains responsible for compliance, including the conduct of its Lending Service Providers (LSPs). RBI – Digital Lending Directions, 2025

Investor note: RupeeRise is fictional. No actual revenue, customer base, loan portfolio, market share or valuation is being claimed. This brief describes the market context, not proven company performance.
